    },
    {
      "claim_id": "hdr-capture",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "wiki-hdri",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-f41c52103f5f"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-f41c52103f5f",
          "exact": "In photography and videography, a technique, commonly named high dynamic range (HDR) allows the dynamic range of photos and videos to be captured beyond the native capability of the camera. It consists of capturing multiple frames of the same scene but with different exposures and then combining them into one, resulting in an image with a dynamic range higher than the individually captured frames."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-f41c52103f5f",
          "subject": "HDR technique in photography and videography",
          "predicate": "captures dynamic range beyond native capability by",
          "object": "capturing multiple frames of the same scene with different exposures and combining them into one, yielding dynamic range higher than individually captured frames"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "VAL-001"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文 [147,190) 表明 HDR 使动态范围可被捕捉到超出相机原生能力之上，对应 claim 的“超出相机原生能力”；[206,279) 表明其方式是拍摄同一场景多帧但曝光不同，对应“拍摄同一场景多帧不同曝光”；[288,312) 与 [313,401) 表明合并为一帧并得到高于单帧的动态范围，对应“再合并，得到高于单帧的”。claim 全部要素在引文中均有直接支撑；引文同时涵盖摄影与摄像，而 claim 仅述及摄影，属子集关系而非矛盾，判定为 supported。",
